Team,

Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

Analytics has been asked to report campaign success, but selected customers m=
ay already have been more likely to convert. The possible stories are that th=
e campaign creates incremental response, that service problems suppress other=
wise suitable offers, or that targeting explains the apparent lift.

We looked at a version of this before. For the October 2020 review, please sh=
ow what changed and whether the earlier conclusion still holds. Failure anecd=
otes are beginning to drive decisions, although retries and late posting may =
be making the problem look larger than the affected-customer population. Ther=
e are enough data exceptions to make a polished average dangerous; preserve t=
he unresolved cases.

Please prepare a control view with the exceptions, owner and reason each item=
 was included. The output must help us decide the treatment, control, success=
 window and guardrail measures before the next campaign launches.

Data available: campaign design and customer responses; monthly account snaps=
hots, status events, limits, product enrolments and signatories; transaction-=
level timestamps, channels, amounts, statuses and error context; customer con=
tacts, complaints and suggestions.

Please state the limitation plainly: Historical campaign responses alone do n=
ot identify causal impact where no comparable control group exists.

